# Single source of truth for the lint toolchain. CI reads this file, and so does
# scripts/lint.sh, so a local run and the Lint job cannot drift apart.
#
# Why both versions are pinned, not just the linter:
#
# golangci-lint bundles its linters, so its version decides which rules exist at
# all. A NEWER local version can report FEWER problems than CI — gosec's G704
# and G117 checks fire on v2.10.1 and not on v2.13.1, so a clean local run said
# nothing about whether the Lint job would pass.
#
# The Go version matters for the same reason in reverse: a golangci-lint binary
# built against one Go release crashes when it analyses source under a much
# newer one. v2.10.1 is built with Go 1.26 and panics under Go 1.27, so pinning
# the linter alone is not enough to reproduce CI.
#
# To upgrade: change a version here, run scripts/lint.sh, fix what the new
# version reports, and commit both the version bump and the fixes together.

GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION=v2.10.1
GO_VERSION=1.26
